SOCIO-ECONOMIC IMPACTS
Introduction
Development of the Westmoreland leases on Tracts II and III will substantially change the socio-economic base and patterns of certain parts of Big Horn County. The purpose of this section is to assess the probable consequences of these changes. This analysis has been drawn primarily from a report prepared by Mountain West Research, Inc. for Westmoreland Resources entitled Economic Impacts Assessment Summary Report, dated February 16, 1976.
